{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-fable-5-2", "id": "msg_011CguUEzXnr6241FkW7RakM", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The logits are very sharp (median |H−A| gap 5–12), so decode ≈ argmax: the decoder is hardly doing anything, the network itself fixes the spell structure. On DFL it is over-confident (mean max prob 0.95 vs 0.89 accuracy). Let me look at the anatomy of the errors on DFL: for each true run, what was predicted, the mean logit margins, and ball visibility.\n\n```python\nL = \"HAD\"\ndef timeline(name, maxlines=95):\n    d = D[name]; y = d[\"y\"]; pred = d[\"pred\"]; lg = d[\"logits\"]; x = d[\"x\"]\n    lines = []\n    for s, e, lab in runs(y):\n        seg = pred[s:e]\n        fr = [(seg == k).mean() for k in range(3)]\n        okfrac = fr[lab]\n        # margin of true label vs best other, mean\n        other = np.max(np.delete(lg[s:e], lab, axis=1), axis=1)\n        marg = lg[s:e, lab] - other\n        flag = \"\" if okfrac > 0.8 else (\"  <<< MISSED\" if okfrac < 0.5 else \"  < partial\")\n        lines.append(\"%6.1fs %s %5.1fs pred H%.2f A%.2f D%.2f  margin mean %+5.1f min %+5.1f  seen %.2f%s\" % (\n            s / 25, L[lab], (e - s) / 25, fr[0], fr[1], fr[2], marg.mean(), marg.min(), x[s:e, 0].mean(), flag))\n    return lines\n\nls = timeline(\"dfl2\")\nbad = [l for l in ls if \"<\" in l]\nprint(len(ls), \"gt runs; flagged\", len(bad))\nprint(\"\\n\".join(ls[:90]))\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2721, "cache_read_input_tokens": 17013, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2721}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "session_id": "id-00000000", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T15:18:20.898Z", "req